Native Guix templates apply network sysctls through
qubes-network-sysctl-service-type, not systemd-sysctl.  Replace the
systemd-sysctl invocation in setup-ip with a no-op so the script keeps working
without systemd.

Guix-specific: no systemd; sysctls applied by the Shepherd service.
Upstream file: qubes-core-agent-linux network/setup-ip

diff --git a/network/setup-ip b/network/setup-ip
index 7ee3c2d..967b46b 100755
--- a/network/setup-ip
+++ b/network/setup-ip
@@ -240,7 +240,7 @@ if [ "$ACTION" == "add" ]; then
 
         primary_dns=$(/usr/bin/qubesdb-read /qubes-primary-dns 2>/dev/null) || primary_dns=
         secondary_dns=$(/usr/bin/qubesdb-read /qubes-secondary-dns 2>/dev/null) || secondary_dns=
-        /lib/systemd/systemd-sysctl \
+        : \
             "--prefix=/net/ipv4/conf/all" \
             "--prefix=/net/ipv4/neigh/all" \
             "--prefix=/net/ipv6/conf/all" \
